  "source_and_output_review": [
    {
      "rule": "A persisted stop follows exact recovered local ownership; a lost acknowledgement cannot leave an owned process unsignalled or authorize another dispatch.",
      "files": [
        "lib/execution.mjs",
        "lib/run.mjs",
        "lib/control.mjs",
        "lib/tick.mjs",
        "lib/task_prepare.mjs",
        "docs/execution.md"
      ],
      "boundaries_checked": [
        "Reconciliation matches the run ID before adopting local acceptance and persists that ownership before invoking the existing requestRunCancellation helper.",
        "Supported pending stops initiate even when job.killed is absent. Existing killed runs retain the five-second killAfter fallback and validated process identities across restart.",
        "Mismatched current runs, unsupported controls and unavailable process inspection do not signal; inspection failure remains visibly pending with RUN_STOP_UNVERIFIED.",
        "Read-only current/inspect never signals or dispatches. Reconciliation performs one launch/operation and preserves confirmation, late-result quarantine and exact cancelled/137 evidence.",
        "Operator stops remain fenced. Only confirmed local implementation timeout releases its temporary fence; preparation and remote controls keep their existing rules. Native cleanup stops only the test-owned process."
      ],
      "regressions": [
        "lost local launch acknowledgement recovers an existing stop before shutdown and cannot redispatch",
        "coordinator reconciliation resumes an owned local kill fallback after restart without another control",
        "local timeout fences survive failed inspection, changed ownership and concurrent operator cancellation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "rule": "Permanently rejected publication inputs settle once through the canonical needs-human lane; collection and unavailable I/O remain pending, and only explicit correction starts another turn.",
      "files": [
        "lib/execution_result.mjs",
        "lib/repository_files.mjs",
        "lib/tick.mjs",
        "lib/control.mjs",
        "lib/commands/resume.mjs",
        "lib/git.mjs",
        "lib/gh.mjs",
        "docs/execution.md"
      ],
      "boundaries_checked": [
        "Repository/branch/input ownership, malformed manifests, unsafe paths, aliases, hashes, modes, authoritative outcomes and public text use existing validators before mutation.",
        "Deterministic EXECUTION_RESULT publication validation writes reason result-validation and phase blocked, preserving prior fingerprint, paths, applied head and real evidence. Replay checks the blocked checkpoint before validation or application.",
        "Collection protocol errors, unavailable/malformed tracked metadata, unavailable mode metadata and ordinary coded filesystem/Git errors do not create a deterministic validation block. Transient fixture failures recover without another submission.",
        "The tick settles only after a durable blocked checkpoint, retaining the provider exit, nullable cost, denials and session. Missing checkpoint durability leaves the entry unresolved.",
        "Repeated progress/review polling and restart preserve one cached result and one needs-human notification, with no publication or automatic continuation; unrelated review reaches done.",
        "Queued and fresh PR rechecks stay refused. Safe operator messages name result-application.json, result.json and any verification.json; explicit same-session resume creates one new owned root and retains rejected bytes.",
        "Concurrent cancellation stays quarantined and cannot become a corrective publication block. Verification failure/interruption, strict clean-tree checks, credential-free POSIX execution, saved evidence and Git/PR cleanup remain canonical.",
        "Valid authentication artifacts still preserve exact bytes and publish with real command evidence. Invalid fixture hashes now remain blocked instead of being modified and replayed in place."
      ],
      "regressions": [
        "deterministic publication rejection settles once and permits an explicit corrective continuation",
        "collection and unavailable publication I/O remain pending and recover without another dispatch",
        "a rejected result cannot settle until its blocked checkpoint is durable",
        "collected authentication source preserves exact artifact bytes through restart and publication",
        "failed remote verification survives polls and restart, settles workflow and permits explicit correction",
        "pushed and verified recovery reject tracked aliases without verification or publication"
      ]
    }
  ],
